  "S1-07": "collate_hebrew word boundaries: byte, nfd and accent_stripped matches have no Hebrew letter or combining mark beside them; skeleton matches have no Hebrew letter beside them. The normalizer inherits them, and its book-wide Qere scope is unchanged (R4-i).",
  "S1-06": "citation_sweep REF HEBREW arm: runs inside a ref entry bind to that entry's own (first) ref, with walk()'s collate, raw-note Qere and in-sentence K/Q keyword functions [CWO-EZ-16]",
